those packages (together, the "Ketupa Products"). It does not license Ansys,
Cadence, Python, open-source dependencies, customer inputs, or other third-party
materials. Separately identified third-party materials retain their own terms.
A written commercial agreement or order signed by the copyright holder may
grant additional rights and controls if it conflicts with this evaluation EULA.
The activation file or entitlement controls the technical term and features;
it is not a substitute for this agreement.
Rights already granted under an earlier license for a copy obtained before
this EULA was published remain in effect for that copy.

2. Evaluation license
Subject to compliance with this EULA and a valid entitlement where required,
you may download, install, and run the Ketupa Products for personal learning,
research, and internal non-production evaluation, including evaluation within
a company. You may edit the Demo's main.py, exposed script/ files, and your own
input data for those purposes. You may retain the engineering results you
generate, subject to any rights in the inputs and third-party tools. You may
share an unmodified copy of the Demo with this EULA and all notices intact.
This permission does not authorize redistribution of the separate Runtime
installers or commercial solver components, except where the copyright holder
expressly permits it in writing. GitHub's ordinary view and fork functions
remain subject to GitHub's applicable terms.

3. Restrictions and ownership
The Ketupa Products are licensed, not sold. No core source-code license or
obligation to supply source is granted for proprietary native components.
Without prior written permission, you may not use them for commercial
production or paid client delivery, sell or sublicense them, distribute
modified Demo copies, redistribute the Runtime or proprietary solver
components, or offer them as a hosted service. Except where mandatory law
expressly permits otherwise, you may not reverse engineer, decompile,
disassemble, or modify proprietary native components, recover their source,
or bypass their integrity, activation, or entitlement checks. All rights not
expressly granted are reserved.

4. Third-party rights and trademarks
Open-source components bundled with a Runtime remain under their own licenses;
nothing in this EULA narrows rights granted by those licenses. Keep applicable
